{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1485329595,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMDMwMzE5MzE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1217","origin":"github"},"title":"Provide `diff` command","message":"We need `diff`. We currently use GitPython's diff, but it is kinda heavy and not flexible enough (e.g. direct mode submodules). We also need `status`, but `status` is pretty much a diff (ignoring the patch generation) of the workdir against HEAD. Ideally, we would like to have enough flexibility to also be able to do as little as `ls` (with recursion).\n\nPlan (based on #1506):\n\n- [x] wrap `git diff --raw SOMETHING`, where SOMETHING is anything that Git supports\n- [x] provide results via a generator that yields annotated paths (`git diff` readily informs us about the pre/post nature of any path...)\n- [x] support recursion in the standard fashion\n- [ ] re-use `AnnexRepo.get_status()` tests","files":null}]}